1
00:00:01,870 --> 00:00:03,990
Show yourself, Leon!

2
00:00:22,080 --> 00:00:25,040
<u>Reborn</u>

3
00:00:22,080 --> 00:00:25,040
to Master the Blade
     From Hero-King to Extraordinary Squire

4
00:00:22,080 --> 00:00:25,040
to Master the Blade
From Hero-King to Extraordinary Squire

5
00:01:38,070 --> 00:01:43,030
Episode 3   Setting Out for the Capital

6
00:01:39,500 --> 00:01:40,450
Yo.

7
00:01:41,400 --> 00:01:43,420
<i>Is that an Artifact?</i>

8
00:01:43,780 --> 00:01:45,950
Do you mean to betray us?

9
00:01:45,950 --> 00:01:48,380
Something like that, yes.

10
00:01:48,820 --> 00:01:55,330
When you said you'd lick a Highlander's 
boots if you had to, that wasn't a joke?

11
00:01:49,810 --> 00:01:55,330
<i>Is he planning to stop us from hurting Rahl 
as a way to win the Highlander's favor?</i>

12
00:01:55,590 --> 00:01:58,480
Don't be stupid. Of course it was a joke.

13
00:01:58,480 --> 00:02:00,800
I'm a holy knight, you know.

14
00:02:01,360 --> 00:02:05,850
I'm ready to throw away my life 
for the people of this nation.

15
00:02:06,330 --> 00:02:07,520
You saw what happened, right?

16
00:02:08,140 --> 00:02:10,010
Right now, the Highlanders can do

17
00:02:10,010 --> 00:02:13,250
whatever they want, and no one 
on the surface can stop them.

18
00:02:14,370 --> 00:02:17,160
It's a holy knight's duty 
to protect the people, right?

19
00:02:17,160 --> 00:02:20,740
But I can't do shit. And it makes me sick.

20
00:02:21,100 --> 00:02:23,960
But without the Highland's help,

21
00:02:23,960 --> 00:02:26,450
we can't protect the surface nations 
from the magicite beasts!

22
00:02:26,790 --> 00:02:28,800
There's some things 
we just have to accept...

23
00:02:29,300 --> 00:02:30,910
I don't like that.

24
00:02:31,350 --> 00:02:35,660
I don't want either the Highlanders or the 
magicite beasts hurting innocent people.

25
00:02:35,660 --> 00:02:37,120
And there's a way to stop them?

26
00:02:37,790 --> 00:02:40,450
Ever heard of the Bloodchain Brigade?

27
00:02:40,450 --> 00:02:41,090
No.

28
00:02:41,490 --> 00:02:44,110
An anti-Highland guerrilla organization.

29
00:02:44,110 --> 00:02:47,750
In other countries, Highlanders 
have destroyed entire towns

30
00:02:47,750 --> 00:02:49,800
after the Brigade killed 
one of their number.

31
00:02:50,150 --> 00:02:52,530
All they do is spread chaos!

32
00:02:52,530 --> 00:02:55,510
You're only seeing one side of the story.

33
00:02:55,780 --> 00:02:58,080
The real goal of the Bloodchain Brigade

34
00:02:58,080 --> 00:03:03,230
is to turn their blood to chains of iron 
and drag the Highland down to earth.

35
00:03:03,230 --> 00:03:04,920
So you'll defeat the Highlanders,

36
00:03:04,920 --> 00:03:08,870
steal their technology, and spread 
it among the people on the surface?

37
00:03:08,870 --> 00:03:11,120
You're a smart one.

38
00:03:11,120 --> 00:03:13,670
That way, we can keep ourselves safe 
from the magicite beasts

39
00:03:13,670 --> 00:03:16,210
without needing to suck up 
to the Highlanders to do it.

40
00:03:16,210 --> 00:03:18,080
The ideal outcome, don't you think?

41
00:03:18,430 --> 00:03:20,620
And that's why you decided to betray us?

42
00:03:20,620 --> 00:03:23,180
They've been trying to 
recruit me for a while,

43
00:03:23,180 --> 00:03:25,550
and what happened tonight 
was the push I needed.

44
00:03:25,550 --> 00:03:28,050
You can't fight the Highland and win!

45
00:03:28,850 --> 00:03:32,520
And that's why I wanted 
to bring you with me.

46
00:03:33,400 --> 00:03:35,510
If they can get a Hyral Menas to research,

47
00:03:35,510 --> 00:03:38,940
they might be able to discover how to make 
Artifacts without the Highlanders' help.

48
00:03:38,940 --> 00:03:39,860
No.

49
00:03:40,170 --> 00:03:43,660
I refuse to take part in something that will 
lead countless people to their deaths!

50
00:03:43,660 --> 00:03:45,930
Want to come with me, Inglis?

51
00:03:45,930 --> 00:03:47,420
I must decline.

52
00:03:47,870 --> 00:03:50,320
So you're like Eris? You want 
to keep things as they are?

53
00:03:50,700 --> 00:03:57,540
Nope! But the way I see it, if I side with 
Eris, I might get a chance to fight you!

54
00:03:58,650 --> 00:04:01,250
S-She's crazy...

55
00:04:01,540 --> 00:04:04,300
I can understand what you're saying.

56
00:04:04,300 --> 00:04:08,780
But I've stopped connecting 
power with justice.

57
00:04:08,780 --> 00:04:12,210
<i>I've lived one life that way already.</i>

58
00:04:12,570 --> 00:04:16,200
If you want to take Eris, come and get her!

59
00:04:16,650 --> 00:04:19,370
I saw enough of that last fight 
to tell you're strong.

60
00:04:19,370 --> 00:04:22,400
It's hard to believe a cute little girl 
can be so tough.

61
00:04:22,840 --> 00:04:27,350
As an adult, I should go easy on you, 
but I'll give you all I've got!

62
00:04:29,090 --> 00:04:29,780
Be careful!

63
00:04:30,160 --> 00:04:33,240
That's a high-rank Artifact that Leon's got!

64
00:04:33,240 --> 00:04:36,740
It has a gift that allows it 
to command lightning beasts!

65
00:04:40,460 --> 00:04:41,920
<i>By my eye, about thirty.</i>

66
00:04:41,920 --> 00:04:44,160
Two of you, follow me.

67
00:04:44,160 --> 00:04:46,380
The rest, go get Inglis.

68
00:04:47,650 --> 00:04:50,090
<i>Eris is injured.</i>

69
00:04:50,400 --> 00:04:54,050
<i>He means to stall me, and then spirit 
her away while I am thus occupied.</i>

70
00:04:54,050 --> 00:04:55,790
<i>A shrewd stratagem!</i>

71
00:04:59,080 --> 00:05:03,650
If you hit them with a strong attack, 
they'll explode!

72
00:05:04,070 --> 00:05:06,760
You sliced it in half? From that distance?

73
00:05:06,760 --> 00:05:09,490
Next time we fight, use that skill!

74
00:05:09,490 --> 00:05:10,590
No!

75
00:05:10,590 --> 00:05:13,460
I'm not like you! 
I don't fight because I enjoy it!

76
00:05:15,420 --> 00:05:18,530
You can't fire that one off 
that often, can you?

77
00:05:18,530 --> 00:05:21,810
You used it just to tell 
Inglis to be careful, huh?

78
00:05:21,810 --> 00:05:23,870
That was nice of you.

79
00:05:23,870 --> 00:05:25,650
So you're a tsundere, huh?

80
00:05:25,650 --> 00:05:26,800
Shut up!

81
00:05:26,800 --> 00:05:28,090
Oh, I hadn't realized!

82
00:05:28,550 --> 00:05:30,560
Hang on! I'll come help you!

83
00:05:46,210 --> 00:05:48,630
Idiot! I just said...

84
00:05:55,390 --> 00:05:56,940
Wh-What happened?

85
00:05:56,940 --> 00:05:58,070
What's going on?

86
00:05:58,460 --> 00:06:00,590
I figured it out, Eris!

87
00:06:00,590 --> 00:06:03,770
If you can't dodge their 
explosions at close range,

88
00:06:03,770 --> 00:06:05,960
then you just need to boost 
your defense so much...

89
00:06:09,350 --> 00:06:11,640
that the explosions don't hurt you, right?

90
00:06:11,640 --> 00:06:14,600
I was trying to tell you 
to attack from a distance!

91
00:06:14,600 --> 00:06:16,610
This is faster, though!

92
00:06:17,660 --> 00:06:21,390
<i>I can surround myself with waves of 
compressed aether—an Aether Shell—</i>

93
00:06:21,390 --> 00:06:24,770
<i>to absorb the blast wave from the explosions!</i>

94
00:06:30,500 --> 00:06:31,990
Sorry to keep you waiting!

95
00:06:32,330 --> 00:06:34,110
You're dreadful.

96
00:06:34,110 --> 00:06:38,340
How could you tell me to use my full strength
when you weren't using yours?

97
00:06:38,340 --> 00:06:39,960
That's not true.

98
00:06:40,820 --> 00:06:44,170
<i>The flaw in this technique is that 
it can't be maintained for long.</i>

99
00:06:44,170 --> 00:06:46,700
You're incredible, kid.

100
00:06:46,700 --> 00:06:51,480
I don't think either Eris or I 
could handle you alone.

101
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:55,640
Which means you're a monster 
on par with a Prismer.

102
00:06:56,090 --> 00:07:00,330
Yes! I'm training to get to the point 
where I can defeat one on my own!

103
00:07:00,330 --> 00:07:01,660
Are you serious?

104
00:07:02,690 --> 00:07:04,570
It's good to dream big!

105
00:07:04,570 --> 00:07:06,000
Maybe you'll be invincible in the future,

106
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:08,110
but for now, I'm just going to 
hope that you've got a weakness.

107
00:07:08,830 --> 00:07:14,570
For example, you can't keep that little 
trick of yours up for long, can you?

108
00:07:14,810 --> 00:07:18,560
<i>He's sharp. And strong of conviction.</i>

109
00:07:18,560 --> 00:07:21,330
<i>In my previous life, he would have 
been one of my most trusted men.</i>

110
00:07:21,760 --> 00:07:23,540
And if that's true?

111
00:07:23,800 --> 00:07:27,080
What else? We see who breaks first!

112
00:07:30,120 --> 00:07:31,470
Not happening.

113
00:07:31,780 --> 00:07:33,070
Seriously?

114
00:07:33,740 --> 00:07:37,400
It's not nice to stare at a girl's legs.

115
00:07:38,240 --> 00:07:40,220
You're the one shoving them in my face!

116
00:07:45,280 --> 00:07:48,100
I said, not happening!

117
00:07:52,380 --> 00:07:53,530
Rani!

118
00:08:05,270 --> 00:08:06,800
A magicite beast!

119
00:08:14,680 --> 00:08:15,630
Rani!

120
00:08:15,630 --> 00:08:16,640
<i>I won't let her be harmed!</i>

121
00:08:17,160 --> 00:08:19,500
<i>I will protect Rani, no matter what!</i>

122
00:08:20,100 --> 00:08:25,570
<i>To master the blade, I decided to 
live this life beholden to none...</i>

123
00:08:26,160 --> 00:08:29,270
<i>But this is the one promise I made to myself!</i>

124
00:08:33,990 --> 00:08:36,740
<i>My vow as "Inglis Eucus"!</i>

125
00:08:38,410 --> 00:08:40,190
Rani, are you okay?

126
00:08:41,180 --> 00:08:43,590
Thank you, Chris!

127
00:08:43,590 --> 00:08:45,420
What are you doing here?

128
00:08:45,420 --> 00:08:49,870
It wouldn't be right to make you 
do this all by yourself!

129
00:08:50,370 --> 00:08:54,100
So I was going to go on ahead 
and teach Rahl a lesson myself.

130
00:08:54,530 --> 00:08:57,300
But when I was inside, waiting,

131
00:08:57,300 --> 00:09:00,700
he suddenly started to scream in pain, 
and then he turned into that thing...

132
00:09:02,550 --> 00:09:04,550
<i>That's Rahl?</i>

133
00:09:04,550 --> 00:09:07,600
Inglis!

134
00:09:07,600 --> 00:09:08,930
<i>That's my name...</i>

135
00:09:09,410 --> 00:09:10,990
But how?

136
00:09:11,440 --> 00:09:14,710
I've never heard of a human 
becoming a magicite beast!

137
00:09:14,710 --> 00:09:17,180
I drugged him.

138
00:09:17,180 --> 00:09:18,380
Leon!

139
00:09:18,380 --> 00:09:20,190
What do you mean?

140
00:09:20,190 --> 00:09:22,160
It's called Prism Powder.

141
00:09:22,590 --> 00:09:26,630
A drug made of condensed 
Prism Flow, they said.

142
00:09:27,040 --> 00:09:29,280
The Bloodchain Brigade created it.

143
00:09:29,280 --> 00:09:32,110
They gave me some last time 
they tried to recruit me.

144
00:09:32,110 --> 00:09:35,240
It's harmless to surface people, 
but if you use it on a Highlander...

145
00:09:35,240 --> 00:09:37,100
Well, you can see for yourselves.

146
00:09:37,400 --> 00:09:39,270
There's no way to cure him?

147
00:09:39,270 --> 00:09:40,980
Of course not.

148
00:09:40,980 --> 00:09:43,820
He deserves a miserable death, in any case.

149
00:09:44,550 --> 00:09:47,920
Anyway, I'll be going.

150
00:09:47,920 --> 00:09:51,730
Between you and Inglis, he's no threat.

151
00:09:52,100 --> 00:09:53,200
Explode!

152
00:09:59,080 --> 00:10:01,400
He got away.

153
00:10:01,400 --> 00:10:03,480
What's going on?

154
00:10:03,480 --> 00:10:04,970
Why is Leon...

155
00:10:04,970 --> 00:10:06,590
I'll explain later.

156
00:10:06,590 --> 00:10:09,540
Inglis!

157
00:10:09,820 --> 00:10:13,270
<i>It may be what he deserves, but I still 
feel pity seeing him in this state.</i>

158
00:10:13,670 --> 00:10:16,240
I'll at least put you down 
without making you suffer!

159
00:10:17,010 --> 00:10:18,120
Chris!

160
00:10:18,610 --> 00:10:22,340
<i>There's only one way 
to end this in a single strike.</i>

161
00:10:23,510 --> 00:10:27,130
<i>But if were to do that here, 
it would raze not only the mansion</i>

162
00:10:27,130 --> 00:10:28,770
<i>but also a large chunk of the town.</i>

163
00:10:29,430 --> 00:10:32,040
<i>Is there a means by which 
the townsfolk may be spared?</i>

164
00:10:39,080 --> 00:10:40,520
<i>That's it!</i>

165
00:10:43,040 --> 00:10:44,780
Rafinha! Inglis!

166
00:10:44,780 --> 00:10:45,800
Are you all right?

167
00:10:45,800 --> 00:10:48,160
Father! You came!

168
00:10:48,160 --> 00:10:51,640
I'm sorry! I was wrong!

169
00:10:51,640 --> 00:10:54,380
I should never have left the two of you 
to shoulder this on your own!

170
00:10:54,680 --> 00:10:59,530
Inglis!

171
00:10:57,700 --> 00:10:58,950
A magicite beast?

172
00:10:58,950 --> 00:11:00,510
Don't let it leave the grounds!

173
00:11:00,510 --> 00:11:01,600
Split up!

174
00:11:01,600 --> 00:11:02,810
Wait!

175
00:11:02,810 --> 00:11:04,900
Eris is going to help us!

176
00:11:05,320 --> 00:11:06,370
Eris!

177
00:11:08,640 --> 00:11:10,270
What are you planning on doing?

178
00:11:10,270 --> 00:11:11,720
Follow my lead!

179
00:11:12,160 --> 00:11:13,440
We'll kick it!

180
00:11:13,440 --> 00:11:15,910
Inglis!

181
00:11:33,920 --> 00:11:36,380
I-It landed all the way out of the city.

182
00:11:36,380 --> 00:11:38,550
Way to go, Eris!

183
00:11:38,550 --> 00:11:39,490
You're so powerful!

184
00:11:39,490 --> 00:11:40,840
What are you saying?

185
00:11:41,190 --> 00:11:43,800
I'm not strong enough to kick it that far.

186
00:11:43,800 --> 00:11:48,280
Follow. My. Lead.

187
00:11:49,710 --> 00:11:51,730
Now, let's finish this!

188
00:11:53,980 --> 00:11:57,800
Inglis!

189
00:11:58,960 --> 00:12:00,520
It's still standing.

190
00:12:00,520 --> 00:12:03,120
What was that you just did?

191
00:12:03,120 --> 00:12:05,380
You made it look like I was 
the one who kicked it...

192
00:12:05,690 --> 00:12:09,100
Chris doesn't want people 
knowing about her power.

193
00:12:09,100 --> 00:12:13,080
If people knew there was somebody who could 
defeat a magicite beast without a Rune,

194
00:12:13,080 --> 00:12:14,950
it would cause chaos, she says.

195
00:12:14,950 --> 00:12:16,300
I see.

196
00:12:16,610 --> 00:12:18,460
<i>That's the excuse I gave her,</i>

197
00:12:18,460 --> 00:12:22,380
<i>but the truth is, I just don't want to be 
stuck with the duty of protecting the town!</i>

198
00:12:23,280 --> 00:12:24,850
So, what do we do?

199
00:12:24,850 --> 00:12:28,350
Eris, is that magicite beast 
as strong as a Prismer?

200
00:12:28,690 --> 00:12:29,610
No.

201
00:12:29,610 --> 00:12:33,790
It's strong, I think, but it's like the 
difference between an adult and a child.

202
00:12:33,790 --> 00:12:38,270
So I need to be able to defeat it in 
one hit if I want to fight a Prismer.

203
00:12:41,310 --> 00:12:42,430
Chris!

204
00:12:41,590 --> 00:12:42,430
What are you doing?

205
00:12:43,720 --> 00:12:45,180
Just watch!

206
00:12:46,410 --> 00:12:49,870
Inglis!

207
00:12:54,590 --> 00:12:56,790
What is that power she's using?

208
00:12:56,790 --> 00:12:58,550
<i>It's been twelve years since then...</i>

209
00:12:59,170 --> 00:13:04,730
<i>This is the perfect chance to test the power 
I've spent this whole time training!</i>

210
00:13:05,750 --> 00:13:09,730
Inglis!

211
00:13:09,730 --> 00:13:12,920
Rahl... Goodbye.

212
00:13:14,590 --> 00:13:15,900
Aether...

213
00:13:15,900 --> 00:13:17,350
Strike!

214
00:13:34,430 --> 00:13:35,870
W-Wow!

215
00:13:36,480 --> 00:13:37,910
That's my Chris!

216
00:13:42,230 --> 00:13:43,540
Chris!

217
00:13:43,540 --> 00:13:44,690
You okay?

218
00:13:45,480 --> 00:13:48,410
I'm a little tired, I think.

219
00:13:48,410 --> 00:13:51,550
I don't have enough stamina. 
Gotta train more.

220
00:13:51,840 --> 00:13:53,640
You're crazy...

221
00:13:53,640 --> 00:13:56,920
What you said was right, Rani.

222
00:13:56,920 --> 00:13:57,820
What did I say?

223
00:13:58,130 --> 00:14:01,270
If you make a wish upon the Highland, 
it'll come true.

224
00:14:01,640 --> 00:14:05,450
Today's fight was a pretty good one.

225
00:14:06,530 --> 00:14:09,250
I'll tell everyone that 
this was Leon's doing,

226
00:14:09,250 --> 00:14:11,400
and that he betrayed us 
for the Bloodchain Brigade.

227
00:14:11,900 --> 00:14:15,360
I'll make sure nobody blames you or Ymir.

228
00:14:15,360 --> 00:14:17,390
Please do!

229
00:14:17,390 --> 00:14:21,790
And tell everyone that it was you 
who defeated the magicite beast, too.

230
00:14:21,790 --> 00:14:25,970
Well, if that's what you want, but...

231
00:14:25,970 --> 00:14:26,580
But?

232
00:14:26,930 --> 00:14:28,540
You owe me one.

233
00:14:28,540 --> 00:14:30,290
Repay that debt someday.

234
00:14:30,290 --> 00:14:32,620
Okay, got it!

235
00:14:33,260 --> 00:14:34,460
Goodbye.

236
00:14:34,460 --> 00:14:36,690
Um, may I ask something?

237
00:14:37,480 --> 00:14:38,860
What is it?

238
00:14:38,860 --> 00:14:43,450
When we were introduced at the party, 
you seemed upset about something.

239
00:14:43,450 --> 00:14:45,050
Why was that?

240
00:14:46,980 --> 00:14:48,620
Sorry.

241
00:14:48,620 --> 00:14:53,070
You may find out someday, 
but I don't want to say it.

242
00:14:53,070 --> 00:14:55,530
I don't want people finding out 
if I can help it.

243
00:15:02,060 --> 00:15:03,910
Here I go, Chris!

244
00:15:03,910 --> 00:15:05,320
Okay, Rani!

245
00:15:15,430 --> 00:15:19,100
Rafinha   Age 15

246
00:15:15,610 --> 00:15:16,960
Wow!

247
00:15:16,960 --> 00:15:19,110
I doubled the number of arrows, too!

248
00:15:19,400 --> 00:15:22,960
Yeah! Your bow's getting 
stronger and stronger!

249
00:15:19,890 --> 00:15:24,310
Inglis   Age 15

250
00:15:22,960 --> 00:15:24,320
It's worth dodging!

251
00:15:24,320 --> 00:15:26,390
What does "worth dodging" mean?

252
00:15:26,390 --> 00:15:29,280
Oh, it's time to go!

253
00:15:29,280 --> 00:15:32,390
No way! I'm not packed!

254
00:15:29,670 --> 00:15:35,710
<i>On this day, 15-year-old Inglis and 
Rafinha would set out for the capital.</i>

255
00:15:32,390 --> 00:15:34,190
Rani, you silly girl.

256
00:15:36,210 --> 00:15:40,910
<i>They were to enroll in the knights' 
academy in the capital city of Kyral.</i>

257
00:15:41,260 --> 00:15:44,150
Take good care of Rafinha.

258
00:15:44,150 --> 00:15:45,640
I will, Your Grace!

259
00:15:45,640 --> 00:15:49,070
If any boys go after her, drive them off!

260
00:15:49,070 --> 00:15:50,560
Leave it to me!

261
00:15:51,130 --> 00:16:00,720
<i>Rafinha would train to be a knight, 
and Inglis, to be her squire.</i>

262
00:16:01,700 --> 00:16:05,070
<i>They would leave behind the home 
they'd known for their whole lives,</i>

263
00:16:05,070 --> 00:16:07,330
<i>and take the month-long 
journey to the capital.</i>

264
00:16:08,150 --> 00:16:11,110
Town of Nova

265
00:16:12,720 --> 00:16:15,810
The ruler of this town is a Highlander?

266
00:16:15,810 --> 00:16:19,020
Yup. They just took over last year.

267
00:16:19,320 --> 00:16:22,130
And they haven't done 
anything terrible, right?

268
00:16:22,130 --> 00:16:23,710
Not at all!

269
00:16:23,710 --> 00:16:27,450
If anything, life's better 
than it was under our last ruler.

270
00:16:27,450 --> 00:16:30,480
All the townspeople are grateful.

271
00:16:30,480 --> 00:16:32,150
I see...

272
00:16:33,140 --> 00:16:37,490
I guess not all Highlanders are bad.

273
00:16:37,490 --> 00:16:38,510
Yeah.

274
00:16:39,440 --> 00:16:41,390
Traveling is so fun!

275
00:16:41,390 --> 00:16:44,030
There's so much good food everywhere!

276
00:16:44,030 --> 00:16:44,900
Yup.

277
00:16:44,900 --> 00:16:48,870
But if we don't cut back a little, 
we're going to run low on funds.

278
00:16:48,870 --> 00:16:53,590
Huh? But it's only been ten days 
since we left Ymir!

279
00:16:53,590 --> 00:16:57,010
This is because you eat so much, Chris.

280
00:16:57,010 --> 00:17:00,970
You too! You eat enough 
for four people every meal!

281
00:17:01,750 --> 00:17:05,740
But without money, we can't 
eat yummy food on our trip!

282
00:17:06,080 --> 00:17:10,100
Why not go help at the castle?

283
00:17:10,100 --> 00:17:11,350
The castle?

284
00:17:11,350 --> 00:17:17,710
Our ruler is hiring knights and mercenaries 
to help with magicite beast attacks.

285
00:17:18,090 --> 00:17:21,670
You two are both knights, 
or so it seems to me.

286
00:17:21,670 --> 00:17:24,240
They're hiring mercenaries, huh?

287
00:17:24,240 --> 00:17:25,860
Sounds like a job for us!

288
00:17:28,360 --> 00:17:30,110
This feels so good!

289
00:17:30,610 --> 00:17:33,320
The hiring exam was easy, huh?

290
00:17:33,320 --> 00:17:34,320
Sure was.

291
00:17:36,350 --> 00:17:40,460
We just had to fight a few knights.

292
00:17:40,460 --> 00:17:43,420
They're giving us the good guest rooms, too!

293
00:17:43,420 --> 00:17:45,860
And the bath is huge!

294
00:17:47,150 --> 00:17:48,360
What's wrong?

295
00:17:48,360 --> 00:17:50,080
No, it's nothing.

296
00:17:51,240 --> 00:17:54,040
<i>Something has been bothering me 
ever since I arrived.</i>

297
00:17:54,040 --> 00:17:56,570
<i>The flow of mana seems strange.</i>

298
00:17:57,500 --> 00:18:02,330
<i>It's like a small amount of mana is being 
drawn away from beneath everyone's feet.</i>

299
00:18:02,330 --> 00:18:04,270
<i>Like it's being drained...</i>

300
00:18:05,220 --> 00:18:07,910
Chris, I'll wash your back!

301
00:18:08,390 --> 00:18:09,690
O-Okay!

302
00:18:11,250 --> 00:18:13,410
You're so lucky, Chris.

303
00:18:13,750 --> 00:18:16,350
You have big breasts, and they're so pretty!

304
00:18:16,350 --> 00:18:18,820
And a nice round butt, too!

305
00:18:18,820 --> 00:18:22,570
Don't say that... It's embarrassing.

306
00:18:22,570 --> 00:18:26,530
I've got the body of a little girl. 
So I'm jealous!

307
00:18:26,530 --> 00:18:28,350
It's not fair.

308
00:18:30,940 --> 00:18:32,990
They're so big and soft!

309
00:18:32,990 --> 00:18:34,730
I wish mine were like that!

310
00:18:33,590 --> 00:18:35,440
Let me go!

311
00:18:35,440 --> 00:18:37,210
You look like you're having fun.

312
00:18:37,210 --> 00:18:38,520
Good evening.

313
00:18:38,520 --> 00:18:40,400
G-Good evening.

314
00:18:43,100 --> 00:18:44,590
What's wrong?

315
00:18:44,590 --> 00:18:46,890
You're a Highlander?

316
00:18:47,250 --> 00:18:50,980
Yes. I'm sorry for not 
introducing myself earlier.

317
00:18:50,980 --> 00:18:53,620
I'm the magistrate of Nova, Seilyn.

318
00:18:53,900 --> 00:18:56,660
"Magistrate"? You're the town's ruler!

319
00:18:56,660 --> 00:18:58,140
I-I'm sorry!

320
00:18:58,140 --> 00:19:00,950
So this bath is for the ruler?!

321
00:19:00,950 --> 00:19:02,330
We didn't know...

322
00:19:02,650 --> 00:19:04,020
It's fine.

323
00:19:04,020 --> 00:19:06,470
I heard that a knight with a Greater Rune

324
00:19:06,470 --> 00:19:11,470
and another warrior had arrived, 
so I wanted to meet them.

325
00:19:11,470 --> 00:19:13,250
Lady Seilyn!

326
00:19:13,250 --> 00:19:16,190
We want to take a bath too!

327
00:19:16,190 --> 00:19:18,060
Rino! Miyumi! Chiko!

328
00:19:18,060 --> 00:19:21,700
You know better than to interrupt 
our ruler when she's talking!

329
00:19:21,700 --> 00:19:23,480
It's alright, Mimoza.

330
00:19:23,480 --> 00:19:24,930
Come in, girls!

331
00:19:24,930 --> 00:19:26,700
Okay!

332
00:19:26,700 --> 00:19:28,140
Me first!

333
00:19:27,600 --> 00:19:29,040
No, me!

334
00:19:28,480 --> 00:19:30,150
Wait!

335
00:19:30,520 --> 00:19:31,760
Those kids...

336
00:19:31,760 --> 00:19:33,730
I know it must be hard for you.

337
00:19:33,730 --> 00:19:39,110
Not at all. I only have a son of my own, 
so it's nice to have little girls around.

338
00:19:40,990 --> 00:19:42,560
Those girls...

339
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:47,170
They're orphans. I couldn't just 
leave them on the streets.

340
00:19:47,170 --> 00:19:48,950
Wow, that's wonderful!

341
00:19:48,950 --> 00:19:51,070
That's how a true ruler should be!

342
00:19:51,070 --> 00:19:52,350
Thank you.

343
00:19:52,350 --> 00:19:55,360
Um, I have a question.

344
00:19:55,360 --> 00:19:56,310
Go ahead.

345
00:19:56,650 --> 00:20:00,350
The flow of mana in this city
seems strange, somehow.

346
00:20:00,350 --> 00:20:01,990
Is there a reason for that?

347
00:20:02,430 --> 00:20:05,060
I'm sorry. I don't know anything about that.

348
00:20:05,060 --> 00:20:06,260
I see.

349
00:20:06,970 --> 00:20:10,610
<i>If there's some powerful warrior 
underground draining everyone's power,</i>

350
00:20:10,610 --> 00:20:12,790
<i>I hope I get to fight them!</i>

351
00:20:13,610 --> 00:20:15,740
How long will you be staying?

352
00:20:16,090 --> 00:20:18,470
We can't stay that long.

353
00:20:18,470 --> 00:20:21,620
We'll be enrolling in the knights' academy 
in the capital.

354
00:20:21,620 --> 00:20:23,190
I see.

355
00:20:23,470 --> 00:20:24,740
Is that a problem?

356
00:20:24,740 --> 00:20:28,090
There's something I'd like your help with.

357
00:20:28,090 --> 00:20:30,160
Just say the word!

358
00:20:30,160 --> 00:20:32,660
If there's something we can help with...

359
00:20:33,410 --> 00:20:39,490
Even if it involves fighting not 
magicite beasts but people?

360
00:20:40,960 --> 00:20:44,360
The knights who served under the 
old ruler were a wicked bunch,

361
00:20:44,360 --> 00:20:47,590
and I fired them all a little while ago.

362
00:20:47,950 --> 00:20:51,740
Their violence toward the 
townspeople had become a problem.

363
00:20:52,300 --> 00:20:58,030
They've all joined together, 
and they seem to be planning something.

364
00:20:58,920 --> 00:21:02,440
Some of the knights I send out 
on patrol have been attacked.

365
00:21:03,160 --> 00:21:06,200
I want to deal with them all at once,

366
00:21:06,200 --> 00:21:09,170
before something happens to 
endanger the townspeople.

367
00:21:09,530 --> 00:21:11,650
I know where their hideout is.

368
00:21:12,180 --> 00:21:13,490
Chris...

369
00:21:13,490 --> 00:21:15,620
There's one hundred, at a minimum.

370
00:21:16,400 --> 00:21:17,410
There he is!

371
00:21:19,160 --> 00:21:23,410
I knew if I caused enough trouble 
in town, you'd come eventually.

372
00:21:23,410 --> 00:21:24,690
Welcome.

373
00:21:24,690 --> 00:21:26,590
Hawker, the last knight commander.

374
00:21:26,590 --> 00:21:27,760
He's the leader.

375
00:21:29,720 --> 00:21:35,180
You can't possibly beat this many, 
Miss High-and-Mighty Highlander.

376
00:21:35,470 --> 00:21:37,130
Quality over quantity!

377
00:21:37,130 --> 00:21:39,960
Chris, preemptive attack!

378
00:21:39,960 --> 00:21:42,350
Don't kill them, okay, Rani?

379
00:21:42,350 --> 00:21:44,120
I'll just blow them all away!

380
00:21:44,970 --> 00:21:48,670
Wh-What? A Greater Artifact?

381
00:21:48,940 --> 00:21:49,860
Burst!

382
00:21:52,940 --> 00:21:55,680
Sorry. I'm going to have to take you down.

383
00:21:58,060 --> 00:22:01,950
Lament your own poor fortune 
that I happened to be here today.

384
00:22:05,620 --> 00:22:09,110
<i>This intensity... It's just like Eris!</i>

385
00:22:10,180 --> 00:22:11,880
<i>She's a Hyral Menas!</i>

